Cell["\<\
matrixModulation is a periodic matrix-valued function of a dimensionless \
angle. Its dimensions are inferred by evaluating it at 0.123.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->810912614,ExpressionUUID->"3398ce03-4ec1-6947-8704-32afc877834f"],

Cell["\<\
Returns two rank-4 tensors with axes {internalRow, internalColumn, photonRow, \
photonColumn}. Photon indices run from -m through m.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->267185291,ExpressionUUID->"6f411701-644a-8144-913f-e696b15557de"],

Cell["\<\
For distinct sites, the first tensor contains Fourier coefficients at \
columnIndex-rowIndex and the second is zero. For coincident sites, the first \
is the internal/photon identity tensor and the second includes the Fourier \
tensor and the diagonal -photonIndex omega shift.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1617021578,ExpressionUUID->"8288b952-463c-2344-9bd1-034549e99b6f"],

Cell["\<\
Coincidence is detected using a distance threshold of 1.*^-5. Combine the \
tensors with PhotonDressTensor.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->290624635,ExpressionUUID->"91143776-49b2-ae49-b4c9-dd01f1133c26"],

Cell["\<\
Uses NIntegrate with default AccuracyGoal -> 10 and Method -> \"LocalAdaptive\
\"; accepts NIntegrate options.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1187766575,ExpressionUUID->"f192132a-423c-f84d-9e65-5122c595e7c5"]
}, Closed]],

